{
  "title": "An Xbox outage has been preventing some games from launching since last night.",
  "publication_date": "2026-07-27T15:03:03+00:00",
  "summary": "An Xbox Live outage reported at 11PM has been blocking some account sign-ins and preventing games from launching since last night, including Game Pass titles that return a license verification error (0x87e107df). The Xbox status page lists the issue as ongoing and the last update from @XboxSupport was three hours ago. Users are advised to monitor official channels for fixes.",
  "content": "After a PS5 outage last week, now it\u2019s apparently Xbox\u2019s turn for problems, weeks after a massive wave of layoffs. The Xbox Live status page says an outage was first reported at 11PM last night and is still ongoing, preventing some account sign-ins and stopping people from playing their games, whether from a disc or a digital copy.\\n\\nOn my home Xbox, I could launch many games I own, but trying to load Game Pass titles threw up a \"Check back later\" message or error code 0x87e107df, indicating the license couldn\u2019t be verified. The last update from @XboxSupport came three hours ago.\\n\\nThe outage appears to affect license verification and sign-in services rather than hardware, meaning both retail disc copies and digital purchases may be blocked until Microsoft resolves the backend issue. Users trying to play Game Pass titles report being unable to verify entitlements, which prevents title launch even when the game files are present on the console.\\n\\nMicrosoft has not yet posted a detailed timeline for restoring full service. Affected users should check the Xbox Live status page and @XboxSupport for updates, and may need to retry launching affected games later once license verification is restored.\\n\\nAuthor: Richard Lawler",
